# SH-CoW Face-A DEFERRED follow-on: Dict `.get(k).unwrap().field = v`. A
# `Dict[K, V].get(k)` returns `Option[Ref[V]]` per the same auto-borrow-from-get
# ruling as `Vector.get(i)`, so the field store MUST write through to the map's
# value slot (`gorget_map_get`), exactly as `d[k].field = v` (the EIndex arm
# already routes CkDict through `gorget_map_get`). CORRECT output is the
# write-through 99 (Rust gg C + LLVM already do this via `try_resolve_field_place`).
#
# The self-host Face-A increment scoped its new `.get(i).unwrap()` place arm to
# Vector/Deque only (`lower_index_element_ptr_place(..., allow_map=false, ...)`)
# — a Dict base keeps the shared `lower_place_base` fall-through, so the SH still
# resolves this chain to a value COPY and DROPS the write (measured SH = 10).
# Kept in `known_gaps/` (out of the self-host runtime-diff corpus) as an EXPLICIT
# cited lagging lane — never a silent parity WRONG. Promote to top-level when the
# SH place arm flips `allow_map` on for the Dict `.get(k)` chain (the EIndex arm
# already handles CkDict; the follow-on is threading `allow_map=true` through the
# chain arm + confirming `.get(k)` on a Dict resolves the value slot).

struct Blk:
    int term

void main():
    Dict[String, Blk] m = {}
    m.set("a", Blk(10))
    m.get("a").unwrap().term = 99
    print(m.get("a").unwrap().term)   # 99 (write-through) — SH currently drops to 10
    print("done")
